    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4fb1585_cde957f4",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2750,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-08-19T21:04:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should go through S0S3 state on our way back down, which should set HOOK_CHIPSET_SUSPEND. It\u0027s possible to write a power state driver that skips S0S3 (and other intermediate states) and immediately dumps into G3, for example. I think such a driver would be broken though. Taking a quick look at power/*, I didn\u0027t see a recent driver that does this.",
      "parentUuid": "846b7130_2642f868",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2750,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 2750,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "bc98a369db209ac42bf4e9b1810dc747fbf83a34",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4a9e95f_b88158a0",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2891,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-08-18T18:12:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is missing some key functionality that we used to rely on for the \u0027dev\u0027 subcommand. the pd_request_source_voltage() function switches us to a sink if we are currently a source. this function does not. is there any reason we can\u0027t just call pd_request_source_voltage() here, and add setting the ceiling to pd_request_source_voltage()?\n\nalso, this function used to read the voltage limit and print it out if it wasn\u0027t being set. now it doesn\u0027t do a read, it just prints out EC_POWER_LIMIT_NONE if you don\u0027t give it a value to set.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2891,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 2891,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "bc98a369db209ac42bf4e9b1810dc747fbf83a34",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
