        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-08-18T18:25:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As you noted, pd_request_source_voltage() switches us to a sink if we\u0027re currently a source. I don\u0027t think we want to do that for all of our ports whenever we get this command. For example, we could be charging on one port and providing power on another when we get the request to limit power.\n\nHow about if I move this to charge_manager.c and call pd_set_external_power_limit (new function, which I think you were implying is not useful) instead?",
